== ui_card "Flash Helper"
  p.sp-text-muted <code>ui_flash(type, message)</code>

  h3 Philosophy
  p Flash messages provide ephemeral feedback to the user. The `ui_flash` helper integrates with a Stimulus controller to:
  ul
    li Automatically animate the entry of the message.
    li Provide different visual indications for success vs. danger.
    li Handle accessibility roles (alert).

  h3 Arguments
  table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 2rem;"
    thead style="border-bottom: 2px solid var(--sp-border);"
      tr
        th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.5rem;" Name
        th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.5rem;" Type
        th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.5rem;" Description
    tbody
      tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sp-border);"
        td style="padding: 0.5rem;" type
        td style="padding: 0.5rem;" Symbol
        td style="padding: 0.5rem;" The nature of the message: <code>:notice</code> (neutral/success), <code>:alert</code> (danger).
      tr
        td style="padding: 0.5rem;" message
        td style="padding: 0.5rem;" String
        td style="padding: 0.5rem;" The text content to display.

  h3 Real World Scenarios
  
  h4 1. Success Message
  p Triggered after a successful action.
  .sp-card
    .sp-card__body
      == ui_flash :notice, "Changes saved successfully."
      pre style="background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 1rem;"
        code == ui_flash :notice, "Changes saved successfully."

  h4 2. Error Alert
  p Use when something goes wrong.
  .sp-card
    .sp-card__body
      == ui_flash :alert, "Failed to connect to database."
      pre style="background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 4px; margin-top: 1rem;"
        code == ui_flash :alert, "Failed to connect to database."

  h3 Live Demo
  p Click to trigger a toast (simulates a flash message):
  button.sp-btn.sp-btn--primary onclick="window.showToast('Hello World', 'notice')" Trigger Toast
